1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,860
Contoso Hospitality. Procure-to-pay and prime cost, with Cowork and Dynamics 365.

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:08,185
Six thirty a.m. at the receiving dock.

3
00:00:08,185 --> 00:00:16,485
Chef Marco Russo and food and beverage director Sofia Bianchi check the seafood delivery against the purchase order in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain.

4
00:00:16,485 --> 00:00:17,630
Two cases are short.

5
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:21,995
By nine, an invoice agent has matched orders, receipts and invoices.

6
00:00:21,995 --> 00:00:23,482
Most clear on their own.

7
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:29,990
Accounts payable lead Grace Kim sees only the exceptions in Dynamics 365 Finance, each with its evidence.

8
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:34,396
Grace asks Cowork to explain the seafood exception and draft the supplier note.

9
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:35,850
One review, and it is sent.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,659
Monday, eight a.m. General manager Tom Wallace opens his prime cost dashboard in Cowork:

11
00:00:40,659 --> 00:00:45,000
food and labor cost by outlet, the biggest variances, and three suggested actions.

12
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:49,700
Sofia approves new par levels, and Dynamics updates the next orders.

13
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:51,858
Cost control while it still matters.

14
00:00:51,858 --> 00:00:57,212
Dynamics runs the transaction, agents match the paper, and Cowork shows leaders what to do next.

